{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1063947-help-with-a-pack-prologue","id":1063947,"title":"Help with a pack prologue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-17T11:25:50-07:00","id":1063947,"title":"Help with a pack prologue","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hi guys,</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I am running a crossover game, and in this game the players started as a human character and in some point of the game them have gained their templates. there are 2 werewolf among them and they want to form a pack, but i wouldn't like to let them just create a pack as the book said, i want them to look for a totem that would accept a pack made of (Werewolf, vampires and mages).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So what kind of hook and stories would you made for a nice prologue of this pack?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T11:35:57-07:00","id":1063951,"title":"","content":"Are the mages Thyrsus?<br /> <br /> The obvious thing to do seems to be finding a spirit that is harassing the werewolves, vampires or mages, and cut it a deal. It gets free Essence from them in exchange for a benefit, rather than having to spend its energy making life annoying for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:36:34-07:00","id":1065916,"title":"","content":"A common threat is the easiest answer. Tie it to some event, possibly a disaster, that triggers the changes from human to supernatural, then make the threat one that affects the Spirit too giving all of the characters and totem a reason to unite against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}